    <h2>1. Global Fuel Price Overview</h2>
    <p>Across 84 countries and 327 weekly observations from January 2020 to April 2026, global retail fuel markets exhibit a clear hierarchy: petrol commands the highest average price, followed by diesel and LPG. Brent Crude, the global benchmark, averaged <strong>$106.69 per barrel</strong> over the period, ranging from a COVID-19 low of <strong>$47.97</strong> (April 2020) to a 2022 crisis peak of <strong>$130.00</strong> (March 2022).</p>

